# G093 — Mp3 Tagger

*v2. See `mp3-tagger.md` for prose: metadata separate from data,
indexed equality fields vs scanned free-form fields, missing-vs-empty
distinction as first-class, query reified as a data structure.*

---

## Choreographic Case: Vault Music Library

[vault-music-library @music-root
    IN ORDER TO
        build an indexed tag store over the music folder
        answer artist/album/year queries in O(1) via indexes
        and surface files with missing metadata for batch editing

    @store <- [tag-store[new]]
    @mp3s  <- [fs[ls {path: @music-root}]]

    for @file in @mp3s
        @bytes <- [fs[read-bytes {path: @file:path}]]
        @tag   <- [id3[parse {bytes: @bytes}]]
        [tag-store[insert {store: @store,
                            path: @file:path, tag: @tag}]]

    sync @user-events {
        search-artist @name ->
            @matches <- [tag-store[query
                                     {store: @store,
                                      query: {kind: "by-artist",
                                              artist: @name}}]]
            [ui[render-results {paths: @matches}]]

        fix-missing @field ->
            @needs <- [tag-store[query
                                   {store: @store,
                                    query: {kind: "missing-field",
                                            field: @field}}]]
            [ui[show-batch-editor {paths: @needs, field: @field}]]
    }
]

---

## Verb Surface

[tag-store
    new
    insert             {store, path, tag}     ;; refreshes all indexes atomically
    get                {store, path}           ;; || not-found
    remove             {store, path}           ;; cleans all indexes
    query              {store, query}          ;; -> [String] sorted
]

[tag
    missing-fields     {tag}                   ;; -> [String]
]

---

## Distinctive Innate idiom: query as reified data, not function call

[tag-store[query {store: @s, query: @q}]
    @q
        where kind is BY_ARTIST        -> artist-index lookup of @q:artist
        where kind is BY_ALBUM         -> album-index lookup of @q:album
        where kind is BY_YEAR          -> year-index lookup of @q:year
        where kind is YEAR_RANGE       -> scan years in [@q:from, @q:to]
        where kind is TITLE_CONTAINS   -> scan tags for substring @q:needle
        where kind is MISSING_FIELD    -> scan tags where @q:field is none
    results ordered by path ascending
]

The query is a value the caller constructs. New query kinds add
variants, not new methods. Compound And/Or can recurse into sub-
queries to produce the full filter AST every real database has.

## Distinctive Innate idiom: missing vs empty as two `where` states

[tag-store[query {store: @s, query: {kind: "missing-field", field: @f}}]
    @s:tags
        where @f is none             -> include  (user never set it)
        where @f is empty string      -> exclude (user explicitly blank)
        otherwise                     -> exclude (user set a value)
]

`none` (unknown, please fill in) and `""` (deliberately blank) are
different user intents. Collapsing them hides information that UIs
legitimately need to act on.

---

## Demo

[demo
    @s <- [tag-store[new]]

    [tag-store[insert
                 {store: @s, path: "a.mp3",
                  tag: {title: "Aeon", artist: "Björk",
                         album: "Vespertine", year: 2001,
                         genre: "Electronic", track: 1}}]]
    [tag-store[insert
                 {store: @s, path: "b.mp3",
                  tag: {title: "Pagan Poetry", artist: "Björk",
                         album: "Vespertine", year: 2001,
                         genre: "Electronic", track: 3}}]]
    [tag-store[insert
                 {store: @s, path: "c.mp3",
                  tag: {title: "Unplayed"}}]]

    -> [tag-store[query
                    {store: @s,
                     query: {kind: "by-artist", artist: "Björk"}}]]
    ;; -> ["a.mp3", "b.mp3"]

    -> [tag-store[query
                    {store: @s,
                     query: {kind: "missing-field", field: "genre"}}]]
    ;; -> ["c.mp3"]
]
